er at best  this movie is forgettable at worst it's  a tutorial on how not to make a  blockbuster if you can think of a  character from the x-men universe they  probably show up here at some point  spouting some awful catchphrase before  fading back into the special effects or  worse Cyclops who had been central to  the first two movies is killed off early  and it never mentioned again Wolverine  shows up of course but ends up coming  across as oddly neutered and bland grow  those back and then there's the Dark  Phoenix storyline a pivotal arc from the  x-men comics that gets tossed into the  plot with about seven other stories  Jackman did his best with the material  but there was no saving this mutant  monstrosity x-men first class he may not  have had a part in the main story but  Wolverine was definitely memorable in  x-men first class showing up to deliver  one line before disappearing for the  rest of the movie use numerical  instructions Xavier cough it may be  short  even by cameo standards but it may also  be the funniest scene Jackman ever got  to film as a surly superhero although we  can only imagine what he would have said  about those yellow jumpsuits do we  really add to were these x-men  apocalypse unlike his brief cameo in  first class  Jacqueline's appearance in x-men  apocalypse finally lets Wolverine come  loose The Wolverine from the comic books  has always nurtured a darker side which  shows itself in the peak of battle is's  berserker rage the mainstream movies  shied away from this for the most parts  thankfully eight movies in they finally  decided to cut him loose back of the  familiar setting of alkali lake which  played a big part in Wolverines origin  story we see  and acts as a caged animal finally  getting a chance to fight for his  freedom it's a moment of fans of the  comics of waited decades to say while  the rest of the movie is sort of hectic  Jackman's brief moments on-screen is a  revelation and helped lay the groundwork  for what was to come  x-men Days of Future past Wolverine can  be such a tortured character that it's  all the more fun when he gets the chance  to just to loosen up for a minute trying  to save the world seems like an odd time  to crack a smile  but while the stakes are high there's no  doubt the tone in this film is lighter  than some of movie's other outings would  you believe me if I told you I was sent  here from the future sure fans of the  comic can debate the decision to swap  out Kitty Pryde who did all the  time-traveling in the comic book  storyline but sending Wolverine back in  time instead was a smart way to bridge  the original and rebooted x-men casts  x-men this is where it all started and  no one knew if it could work  what would a full blown superhero team  full of wacky powers look like on the  big screen will they wear 4s and spandex  [Music]  we actually go outside nuzens what would  you prefer yellow spandex more  importantly would audiences turn out for  comic book characters that weren't  Superman Batman or spider-man with x-men  those questions were definitively  answered it was faithful to the comics  that adapted but use just enough black  lever to welcome mainstream audiences  into the fold and no one helped carry  the film or capture the imagination of  the audience more than Jackman with his  portrayal of Wolverine an amnesiac  drifter without a past or future will be  was the audience's window into this  world of outcasts and misfits if we  found them weird that was okay because  he did to Jackman became a star the  moment he appeared on screen and  Wolverine proved he could brawl with the  best of them spandex and all the  Wolverine following the undeniable  failure of x-men origins Wolverine  acclaimed director James Mangold was  brought in to clean up the Wolverine  franchise and for two-thirds of the  Wolverine he did just that  crafting a nuanced intimate look at  Logan and drawing heavily on perhaps his  most celebrated comic-book plotline  Chris Claremont and Frank Miller's  Wolverine limited series by rooting the  movie in his grief at the loss of Jean  Grey and temporarily taking away his  healing power the movie shows Wolverine  at his most vulnerable true the third  act then descended into the typical  bloat of a big-budget action movie with  cartoonish robots and CGI heavy fight  scenes but it showed that there were  more Logan stories to tell especially if  you stick to a source material as  closely as possible X to x-men United  the best and the lone x-men movie is  without a doubt x-2 x-men United thanks  largely to its Wolverine centered plot  the franchise took this step forward by  looking to its past specifically the  mysterious background of his most  tortured hero by pitting Logan against  William Stryker the man who coated  Logan's bones with adamantium and turned  his memory into Swiss cheese we got to  see a plot that was both personal and  explosive and essential set pieces  perhaps the best blend of action and  emotion this franchise has ever  delivered when baby sitter Logan hints  at his berserker rage for the first time  on-screen leaves more the first x-men  movies set the stage this is what  elevated the franchise into an  out-and-out hit Logan it only took nine  tries to get it perfect but boy was it  worth the wait this is the Wolverine  we've all been waiting for a grizzled  bastard who isn't looking for a fight  but will definitely finish one if it all  starts loosely inspired by the acclaimed  and influential old man Logan arc it  tells the story of an aged two grieving  veteran of too many superhero battles  who wants to disappear but gets pulled  back in one last time with a hard R  rating that allows the blood and guts  Wolverine is famous for  nobody holds back here not the  filmmakers are not our hero like a  Johnny Cash song come to life  Logan is both poetic and gritty and this  one of the best superhero movies ever  made what's next now that Jackman's  Wolverine has been laid to rest fans  have been speculating about where the  character will go next  considering daphne Keens show-stopping  performance as Laura in Logan it's  possible that she'll become the next  on-screen Wolverine especially since the  same thing has happened in the comics  but the comics also delve into a range  of other scenarios from alternate  universe Wolverines to Logan himself  coming back from the grave in other  words these are comic-book movies  anything's possible  as far as Jacqueline's concerned he  doesn't particularly care who takes up  the adamantium mantle with one exception  as he jokingly told the New York Times  anyone could become the new Wolverine  unless Daniel day-lewis plays him in win  Z Oscar then I might have a little  problem with the Fox Disney merger on  the horizon only time will tell what the  future has in store for Wolverine thanks  for watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to  [Music]
 

